#   .  open        #  wall        O  pit        ^  spikes      H  high ground
#   A  Player A deploy slot       B  Player B deploy slot
#   any other letter = an enemy declared by a 'spawn' line below

id: as-05-the-door
number: 405
name: The Door
description: Two units, eight Husks, one raised doorway flanked by spikes. Numbers stop mattering the moment only one of them can reach you.
design: Asymmetry 5 — lopsided numbers. One unit each, eight Husks.
design: Both players deploy inside the same walled room; that is the point, and it is a lint. The doorway is high ground: anything shoved off it takes fall damage on the way out.
design: The tide, not the headcount: the objective is `survive 8`, so anyone still standing at the end of round 8 wins and killing the last Husk stops being the point. The doorway is the tactic, not the win condition — it is where two units can hold off eight. Arrivals land on the two north corners the starting Husks came from — 0,0 and 6,0 — the far side of the room from the door.

spawn h = Husk

roster a: Vanguard
roster b: Threadcaster

objective: survive 8

wave 3 = h@0,0 h@6,0
wave 6 = h@0,0 h@6,0

